# rule.always.diagnose-reviewer-malfunctions

a `malfunction` is a broken process, not a verdict — the review could not run, or could not be read. diagnose the cause and name the fix; never hand a human a bare *"it broke."*

⚠️ terminal-for-unlock, **and it still blocks passage**. a broken reviewer at l1 does not hold l3 from a run, and the stone cannot pass while it is broken.

| the cause | you |
|---|---|
| **driver-fixable** — a bad glob, an absent supply file, a malformed rubric path, an artifact it could not parse | fix it, re-arrive |
| 🔴 **a context overflow** — the lane's prompt blew the window, so it reviewed naught | re-run the rubric **scoped** — see below |
| **human-fixable** — an absent credential, a permission gate, a foreman-only grant | surface the **exact command**, never the symptom |
| unclear | read its stderr and logs, classify, then route |

## 🔴 the overflowed lane — a task, never a verdict

the guard hardcodes `--diffs since-main`; `rhx review` is not so bound, so the same rubric runs narrowed:

```sh
rhx review --rules '<the lane rubric path>' \
           --paths-with 'src/<subsystem>/**/*.ts' --paths-wout '**/*.test.ts' \
           --output '.review/<iter>.<lane>.scoped.<slug>.md' --goal exhaustive
```

⚠️ **its temptation is unique.** every other malfunction announces itself as broken; an overflowed lane returns terminal and unlocks the next level, so it reads much like a lane that ran. a driver who merely files the overflow removes a lens from the drive.

✅ **the inherited `--diffs since-main` scope is already correct — do NOT re-derive it.** `getAllFileDiffsFromRange.ts` prefers `origin/main` (line 43) and takes `git merge-base` (line 70), so a commit main is ahead on cannot enter the diff. an item the scoped run raises is yours.

one honest diagnosis pass, never a debug spiral: read the logs → classify → act.

if it resists one pass, escalate **with what you found** — the symptom, the logs read, your best read of the cause. a named unknown beats a bare break.

blocker: a malfunction escalated with a bare symptom · a driver-fixable cause handed to a human · an overflowed lane reported upward with no scoped re-run.
